L000314	\label{fig:fields}
L000315	\end{figure}
L000316	
L000317	Figure~\ref{fig:2} shows the NEC lines given by solutions to \eqref{eq:NEC} for LO up to NNNLO for the same example.
L000318	In the center, $x=0$, all curves are close to each other but near the SSH there are differences between these curves. This suggests that the large-$D$ expansion converges fast in the center and slowly at the SSH. The downward bending of the NEC lines observed in numerical simulations \cite{Ecker:2024haw,Ecker:prep} happens not before NNLO.
