L000333	Finally, to LO and NLO the maxima of $f$ are at $f=1$ for all values of $x$. To NNLO we get
L000334	\begin{equation}
L000335	\textrm{max}\,f(\tau,\,x) = 1 - \frac{\epsilon^2}{4}\,\big(1-x^4\big)\,\big(\beta^{\prime}(\tau_0)\big)^2 + \mathcal{O}(\epsilon^3)
L000336	\label{eq:fmax}
L000337	\end{equation}
L000338	where $\tau_0$ is the NEC vertex time. The drop of the maximum of $f$ from $1$ to something proportional to $1/(D-1)^2$ is in qualitative agreement with numerical simulations at moderate values of $D$ \cite{Ecker:prep}.
